THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

JUCE 9 — audio, GUI and plugin wrappers.
  Used under the AGPLv3, the open-source half of its dual licence.
  Section 13 of the GPLv3 grants permission to combine a GPLv3 work with an
  AGPLv3 one and to convey the result; the AGPL's network-interaction clause
  then applies to the combination. Masterpiece offers no network interaction —
  it is built with JUCE_WEB_BROWSER and JUCE_USE_CURL both off — so that
  clause imposes nothing further here.
  https://juce.com/legal/juce-9-licence/

pugixml — XML parsing for the organ-definition loader.
  MIT.  https://github.com/zeux/pugixml

libarchive — reading sample sets straight from their RAR packages.
  BSD-2-Clause.  https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive

unarr — reading solid RAR 4 packages; only its RAR 4 reader is built.
  LGPL-3.0.  https://github.com/selmf/unarr

WavPack — decoding compressed samples.
  BSD-3-Clause.  https://github.com/dbry/WavPack


READ, BUT NOT COMPILED IN
-------------------------

The design owes a debt to four projects. None of their code ships here.

  GrandOrgue    https://github.com/GrandOrgue/GrandOrgue
  OdfEdit       https://github.com/GrandOrgue/OdfEdit
  rusty-pipes   https://github.com/dividebysandwich/rusty-pipes
  HISE          https://github.com/christophhart/HISE
